{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013m9aJBpLPzAZFKZTNVTJ1V","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 05: Checkout and payment\n2\t\n3\t**What to build:** The customer fills in their details on the checkout form (`Your details`), sees validation messages as they go, can go `Back` to the summary and return — or reload — without losing what they typed, and pays with the `Pay <total> PLN` button. Paying sends the reservation to the backend; success opens `/confirmation`, failure keeps the form and shows a toast.\n4\t\n5\t**Specification:** sections 2.1, 2.2 (`POST /reservations`), 3.1, 7, 9.4, 9.7.\n6\t\n7\t**Blocked by:** 04 — Booking and summary.\n8\t\n9\t**Status:** ready\n10\t\n11\t- [ ] AC-41 — The form renders first name, last name, email, confirm email, phone number and a terms checkbox.\n12\t- [ ] AC-42 — First name and last name are required and must be at least 2 characters.\n13\t- [ ] AC-43 — Email is required and must be a valid address; confirm email must match it.\n14\t- [ ] AC-44 — Phone number is optional; when filled it must be exactly 9 digits.\n15\t- [ ] AC-45 — The terms checkbox is required.\n16\t- [ ] AC-46 — The pay button is enabled whenever no payment request is in flight; clicking it on an invalid form marks all fields as touched, shows the messages and shows the toast `The form contains errors`, without navigating.\n17\t- [ ] AC-47 — The pay button on a valid form sends `POST /reservations`, is disabled while the request is in flight, navigates to `/confirmation` on success, and on failure stays on the form and shows the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.`\n18\t- [ ] AC-61 — The checkout shows the title `Your details`.\n19\t- [ ] AC-62 — The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, the total of the booking.\n20\t- [ ] AC-63 — `Back` on the checkout returns to the summary with the booking intact.\n21\t- [ ] AC-64 — The checkout values survive going back to the summary and forward again, and a page reload; a new booking starts with an empty form.\n22\t- [ ] AC-65 — The labels of the five required fields end with `*`; the phone label does not.\n23\t- [ ] AC-68 — Every checkout identifier in section 9.4 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"606c101f-c402-4bc0-9ecd-25b418a05971","uuid":"4d8daec9-183e-493f-bbd6-c53a26810ee4","timestamp":"2026-10-16T09:38:44.286Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/project/spec/tickets/05-checkout.md","content":"# 05: Checkout and payment\n\n**What to build:** The customer fills in their details on the checkout form (`Your details`), sees validation messages as they go, can go `Back` to the summary and return — or reload — without losing what they typed, and pays with the `Pay <total> PLN` button. Paying sends the reservation to the backend; success opens `/confirmation`, failure keeps the form and shows a toast.\n\n**Specification:** sections 2.1, 2.2 (`POST /reservations`), 3.1, 7, 9.4, 9.7.\n\n**Blocked by:** 04 — Booking and summary.\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-41 — The form renders first name, last name, email, confirm email, phone number and a terms checkbox.\n- [ ] AC-42 — First name and last name are required and must be at least 2 characters.\n- [ ] AC-43 — Email is required and must be a valid address; confirm email must match it.\n- [ ] AC-44 — Phone number is optional; when filled it must be exactly 9 digits.\n- [ ] AC-45 — The terms checkbox is required.\n- [ ] AC-46 — The pay button is enabled whenever no payment request is in flight; clicking it on an invalid form marks all fields as touched, shows the messages and shows the toast `The form contains errors`, without navigating.\n- [ ] AC-47 — The pay button on a valid form sends `POST /reservations`, is disabled while the request is in flight, navigates to `/confirmation` on success, and on failure stays on the form and shows the toast `Payment failed. Please try again.`\n- [ ] AC-61 — The checkout shows the title `Your details`.\n- [ ] AC-62 — The pay button reads `Pay <total> PLN`, the total of the booking.\n- [ ] AC-63 — `Back` on the checkout returns to the summary with the booking intact.\n- [ ] AC-64 — The checkout values survive going back to the summary and forward again, and a page reload; a new booking starts with an empty form.\n- [ ] AC-65 — The labels of the five required fields end with `*`; the phone label does not.\n- [ ] AC-68 — Every checkout identifier in section 9.4 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}}}
