t code review.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary request, I was mid-way through browser-driven verification of the already-implemented application using a custom Playwright setup (since no project `run` skill existed and `chromium-cli` wasn't available). I had:\n   1. Installed `playwright-core@1.64.1` in `/tmp/pw-driver` and located the Chromium binary at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome`.\n   2. Started `pnpm api` and `CI=true pnpm nx serve cinescope` as background processes, and — after extensive debugging — determined they only bind to IPv6 `::1`, requiring my test scripts to target `http://[::1]:3000` / `http://[::1]:4200` instead of `localhost`/`127.0.0.1`.\n   3. Ran a full `drive.js` Playwright script (navigating `http://[::1]:4200/`, screenshotting the default empty-day view successfully as `/tmp/shots/01-movie-list-default.png` — which visually confirmed AC-52 and AC-54: day buttons \"TODAY, SATURDAY, SUNDAY, MONDAY, TUESDAY\" plus a datepicker, and \"No screenings on this day\" with no movie cards), then navigating to `http://[::1]:4200/?date=2026-09-15` and waiting for `[data-testid=\"movie-list\"]` — which **timed out after 15000ms**, producing error: `DRIVER ERROR page.waitForSelector: Timeout 15000ms exceeded. ... waiting for locator('[data-testid=\"movie-list\"]') to be visible`.\n   4. Checked for a `02-movie-list-loaded.png` screenshot — it did not exist (confirming the script errored out before reaching that screenshot line).\n   5. Viewed `01-movie-list-default.png` directly (via the Read tool) — confirmed it rendered correctly.\n   6. Wrote and ran a smaller debug probe script `/tmp/pw-driver/probe.js` that navigates to the same `?date=2026-09-15` URL, waits 3 seconds, screenshots to `/tmp/shots/debug.png`, and dumps `page.content()` plus console/requestfailed event logs, to figure out what state the page was actually in (loading/error/empty/loaded) and whether any network requests failed. The command w