{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012kxcXBdTtgmoR7BXnKDsr2","type":"tool_result","content":"Each seat and couch is painted, as its background colour, with the colour of its state:\n\n| State | Colour | Applies to |\n|---|---|---|\n| Available | `#2E7D32` | free regular seats and free couches |\n| Selected | `#F9A825` | any selected seat or couch |\n| Unavailable | `#C62828` | any seat or couch in `occupiedSeats` |\n| Accessible | `#1565C0` | free, unselected accessible seats |\n\nHovering or focusing a seat must not change its background colour.\n\nUnder the auditorium, a legend lists these four states — `Available`, `Selected`,\n`Unavailable`, `Accessible` — each with a swatch of its colour.\n\n### 5.4 Prices\n\n| Seat | Price |\n|---|---|\n| rows 1–5, including the accessible seats | `25.00 PLN` |\n| rows 6–10 | `32.00 PLN` |\n| rows 11–14 | `39.00 PLN` |\n| one couch in row 15 (two seats) | `89.00 PLN` |\n\nPrices are always printed with two decimals and the `PLN` suffix: `25.00 PLN`.\n\n### 5.5 Selected-seats panel\n\nShows the current selection and updates on every click:\n\n```\nSelected seats: 4\nRow 7: 11, 12\nRow 15: 1-2\n```\n\n- The first line is `Selected seats: <n>`, where `<n>` counts seats (a couch counts as 2).\n- Then one line per row that has a selection, rows in ascending order:\n  `Row <r>: <seats>`, the seats in ascending column order, separated by `, `; a seat is its\n  column number, a couch is `<a>-<b>`.\n- With nothing selected the panel shows `Selected seats: 0` and no row lines.\n\n### 5.6 Actions\n\n- `Cancel` clears the booking and opens `/`.\n- `Continue` opens `/screenings/:id/summary`. With no seat selected it does nothing (it may\n  be disabled).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Summary (`/screenings/:id/summary`)\n\nThe screen loads the screening and its movie. If either cannot be loaded, redirect to `/`.\n\nA title `Your tickets`, then one list item per selected seat and one per selected couch,\nordered by row and then by column. Each item shows:\n\n| Field | Content | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| movie | the movie title | `The Silent Harbor` |\n| date and time | `<ISO date> <time>` of the screening | `2026-09-15 16:00` |\n| row | the row number | `7` |\n| seat | a seat: its column number; a couch: `Couch <a>-<b>` | `12` / `Couch 3-4` |\n| price | the price from 5.4 | `32.00 PLN` |\n| — | a `Remove` button | |\n\n`Remove` takes the seat or couch out of the booking; the list and the total update at\nonce. Removing the last item opens `/screenings/:id/seats`.\n\nBelow the list: `Total: <sum> PLN`, the sum of the listed prices with two decimals, e.g.\n`Total: 121.00 PLN`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"606c101f-c402-4bc0-9ecd-25b418a05971","uuid":"54bb9f0c-cbef-4a60-9dde-7237484b485f","timestamp":"2026-10-16T09:57:14.410Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Each seat and couch is painted, as its background colour, with the colour of its state:\n\n| State | Colour | Applies to |\n|---|---|---|\n| Available | `#2E7D32` | free regular seats and free couches |\n| Selected | `#F9A825` | any selected seat or couch |\n| Unavailable | `#C62828` | any seat or couch in `occupiedSeats` |\n| Accessible | `#1565C0` | free, unselected accessible seats |\n\nHovering or focusing a seat must not change its background colour.\n\nUnder the auditorium, a legend lists these four states — `Available`, `Selected`,\n`Unavailable`, `Accessible` — each with a swatch of its colour.\n\n### 5.4 Prices\n\n| Seat | Price |\n|---|---|\n| rows 1–5, including the accessible seats | `25.00 PLN` |\n| rows 6–10 | `32.00 PLN` |\n| rows 11–14 | `39.00 PLN` |\n| one couch in row 15 (two seats) | `89.00 PLN` |\n\nPrices are always printed with two decimals and the `PLN` suffix: `25.00 PLN`.\n\n### 5.5 Selected-seats panel\n\nShows the current selection and updates on every click:\n\n```\nSelected seats: 4\nRow 7: 11, 12\nRow 15: 1-2\n```\n\n- The first line is `Selected seats: <n>`, where `<n>` counts seats (a couch counts as 2).\n- Then one line per row that has a selection, rows in ascending order:\n  `Row <r>: <seats>`, the seats in ascending column order, separated by `, `; a seat is its\n  column number, a couch is `<a>-<b>`.\n- With nothing selected the panel shows `Selected seats: 0` and no row lines.\n\n### 5.6 Actions\n\n- `Cancel` clears the booking and opens `/`.\n- `Continue` opens `/screenings/:id/summary`. With no seat selected it does nothing (it may\n  be disabled).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Summary (`/screenings/:id/summary`)\n\nThe screen loads the screening and its movie. If either cannot be loaded, redirect to `/`.\n\nA title `Your tickets`, then one list item per selected seat and one per selected couch,\nordered by row and then by column. Each item shows:\n\n| Field | Content | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| movie | the movie title | `The Silent Harbor` |\n| date and time | `<ISO date> <time>` of the screening | `2026-09-15 16:00` |\n| row | the row number | `7` |\n| seat | a seat: its column number; a couch: `Couch <a>-<b>` | `12` / `Couch 3-4` |\n| price | the price from 5.4 | `32.00 PLN` |\n| — | a `Remove` button | |\n\n`Remove` takes the seat or couch out of the booking; the list and the total update at\nonce. Removing the last item opens `/screenings/:id/seats`.\n\nBelow the list: `Total: <sum> PLN`, the sum of the listed prices with two decimals, e.g.\n`Total: 121.00 PLN`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
